Park, Hounslow, London"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/355"} "Green Pond Road Stadium, Walthamstow, London"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/356"} "Goldstone Ground, Hove"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/357"} "Fratton Park, Portsmouth"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/33663"} "218 from 18 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The 1948 tournament had two favorites for the title: Sweden and the home team. Great Britain had not played at the Olympics since their " [:a {:href "/results/33530"} "1912"] " victory. Players from England, Scotland, Northern Ireland, and Wales were selected by " [:a {:href "/athletes/5000574"} "Matt Busby"] ", the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/264"} "Manchester United"] " manager (a position he held until 1969). Sweden too was coached by a Briton, " [:a {:href "/athletes/5000902"} "George Raynor"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Britain could not impress during the Olympics, struggling past the Netherlands and France before being eliminated by Yugoslavia. Sweden, by contrast, breezed through the early rounds. In the quarter-finals, South Korea was butchered 12-0. The final saw the best play of the tournament, and Sweden won with a dominant second half, 3-1."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The victorious Swedish team featured three brothers: " [:a {:href "/athletes/27274"} "Bertil"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/27275"} "Gunnar"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/27276"} "Knut Nordahl"] ". The most famous of them was Gunnar, who played for " [:a {:href "/affiliations/121"} "AC Milan"] " after the Olympics, joining fellow gold medalists " [:a {:href "/athletes/27230"} "Gunnar Gren"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/27253"} "Nils Liedholm"] " to form the Italian club’s feared “Gre-No-Li” attack line."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There were originally 23 nations entered. The final draw for the 1948 football tournament looked nothing like the original draw, because of withdrawals. The original draw for the preliminary round was as follows:"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tEgypt vs. Denmark (moved to a first round match)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tIreland vs. Netherlands (match was held)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tBurma (Myanmar) vs. India (Burma withdrew; match scheduled for 26 July at Woodside Road, Worthing, England)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tYugoslavia vs. Pakistan (Pakistan withdrew; match scheduled for 27 July at Southend Stadium, at Southend-on-Sea, England)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tSweden vs. Austria (moved to a first round match)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tChina vs. Turkey (moved to a first round match)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tLuxembourg vs. Afghanistan (match was held)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "The scheduled matches for the first round were as follows:"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tPoland vs. Egypt / Denmark winner (Poland withdrew, Egypt played Denmark)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tGreat Britain vs. Ireland / Netherlands winner (match was held as GBR vs. IRL)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tFrance vs. Burma (Myanmar) / India winner (Burma withdrew; France played India)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tPalestine vs. Yugoslavia / Pakistan winner (Palestine and Pakistan withdrew; Yugoslavia played Luxembourg in round one)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tUnited States vs. Sweden / Austria winner (Sweden played Austria in round one; United States played Italy in round one)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tHungary vs. Italy (Hungary withdrew; Italy played the United States in round one)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tKorea (South) vs. China / Turkey winner (China played Turkey in round one; Korea played Mexico in round one)"] "\n\n" [:p {} "•\tMexico vs. Luxembourg / Afghanistan winner (Luxembourg played Yugoslavia in round one; Mexico played Korea in round one)"] "\n"] [:button {:id "button886596", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button886596').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {:style "